cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AloHEP, please cite the article listed under preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "AloHEP: A Luminosity Optimizer for High Energy Physics"
version: "2.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tobbetuyef/AloHEP"
abstract: >-
  Java application that simulates the interaction region of symmetric and asymmetric
  particle colliders with a slice-based particle-in-cell model (cloud-in-cell charge
  assignment, direct Green's-function potential solve, bicubic force interpolation) and
  computes the luminosity with the hourglass effect, a crossing angle and the beam-beam
  pinch, for any pairing of electrons, positrons, protons, muons and heavy ions.
keywords:
  - luminosity
  - beam-beam interaction
  - hourglass effect
  - asymmetric colliders
  - particle-in-cell
